I checked the source code and (Waaaah!) it's true. The Minotaur scam
no longer works. One can no longer polymorph a wand into a wand of
wishing (or into a wand of polymorph either for that matter). I think
that's a real bummer. My old demigod strategy was to fight my way down
to the castle, snag the wand of wishing in it, and wish for cursed
scrolls of genocide, and polypile until I had about a dozen or so (!)
wands of wishing, which would more than enough enable me to get all
the stuff I want to beat the pants out of the Wiz. Sigh. But (!), as
the astute hacker knows, there are ways from which one can get wishes
other than from a wand of wishing...

... Magic lamps! I checked the code and tried it out, and there is no
code that prevents you from polymorphing a tool into a magic lamp. So
the strategy is as follows: Grab all the tools you can find from as
many dungeon levels as you can reach and put them all in a pile and
polymorph them. Soon you'll get magic lamps. Bless them (holy water
can easily be obtained with a wand of cancellation, a lawful altar,
and a bunch of useless potions.) and #rub the wishes from them. (You
can get two wishes from each lamp by recharging them - wish for 3
blessed scrolls of charging; if you get more than one scroll, then you
can recharge several magic lamps and get several additional wishes for
the price of one.) Occasionally (even if you recharge your polymorph
wand) you will have to wish for a wand of polymorph to keep the pile
going. Of course better success is achieved with a larger pile (Magic
lamps, though yielding only 2 wishes to a wand of wishing's 7, do
appear *much* more often than the wands do - I actually found myself
getting wishes more often from my small tool pile then from my vast
wand polypiles of previous versions.) You may be able to build up your
pile (You can drop your used magic lamps back into the pile) by
wishing for cursed scrolls of genocide and genociding *nymphs*! Nymphs
often carry mirrors, so maybe we can call this the Nymph Scam?

BTW, concerning wishes and ways to get them, I was once playing wizard
in nethack 3.0pl3, and in this a game the WAND I GOT IN MY STARTING
INVENTORY WAS A WAND OF WISHING! No one had modified the code (I know
of course the code checks for wands of wishing and other powerful
items for the wizard), but my question is were they allowed to start
with them in previous versions? There could be a *very* minor bug
then (or now) where they give the wizard a random wand, and if its a
W.O.W. then randomly give him another wand. If there is no loop and by
very good luck the code returns two W.O.W.'s in a row, then the
character could start out with one. Either way, I had just started
playing when I had that game, and so I didn't know how to use the wand
and got killed by a jackal on dlvl1. Oh well...

Happy hacking!

